  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening HIV prevention and reduction of Tuberculosis morbidity and mortality - Botswana (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Botswana, TB/HIV, Botswana-Ministry of Health (Ministry of Health)This program has the following goals: Prevent new HIV infections by 2017.  To reduce morbidity, mortality, psychosocial and economic impact associated with Tuberculosis by 2017. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To reduce the incidence rate of HIV among Batswana by 50% by 2017.  Objective 2: To increase access to HIV and AIDS comprehensive quality treatment, care and support services by 2017.  Objective 3: To strengthen high quality DOTS services in all districts by 2017.  Objective 4: To expand and strengthen TB/HIV and drug resistant TB activities in all districts by 2017.  Objective 5: To improve the ethical and legal environment to support the national response to HIV and AIDS by 2017.  Objective 6: To strengthen community and health systems for quality, comprehensive and sustainable integrated HIV/TB /RMNCH and other co-morbidities services</narrative>
  </description>
